WEBVTT

00:00:20.770 --> 00:00:24.870
Good grief. He sure went
 and did something unnecessary.

00:00:26.530 --> 00:00:29.670
He's a fool who doesn't see the big picture.

00:00:32.260 --> 00:00:33.780
Damn Basara.

00:00:34.030 --> 00:00:39.330
Interfering in the power struggle between
demon realm factions is already unforgivable,

00:00:41.490 --> 00:00:44.110
and yet he actually united them.

00:00:46.170 --> 00:00:50.510
There's Jin, too. Both parent and child 
are taking too much into their own hands.

00:00:50.510 --> 00:00:55.640
Regardless, this a grave matter
 that threatens the survival of the hero village.

00:00:55.640 --> 00:00:59.600
We need careful consideration
 on how to proceed.

00:00:59.600 --> 00:01:01.110
There's no need.

00:01:01.110 --> 00:01:04.480
Any who would harm our duty, 
no matter who they may be...

00:01:05.740 --> 00:01:10.060
We certainly can't afford 
to overlook this any longer.

00:01:12.310 --> 00:01:16.720
If he is going to bring 
about calamity again, then...

00:01:23.750 --> 00:01:26.340
How is this, Basara-sama?

00:01:27.220 --> 00:01:27.860
Huh?

00:01:27.860 --> 00:01:30.320
Oh, well, it does feel good.

00:01:31.380 --> 00:01:34.840
Am I bothering you, Basara-sama?

00:01:34.840 --> 00:01:37.260
No, you're not.

00:01:37.700 --> 00:01:38.870
I'm glad.

00:01:51.100 --> 00:01:53.330
Enough moaning, Zest!

00:01:55.960 --> 00:01:56.650
Huh?!

00:01:58.200 --> 00:01:59.260
Mio?!

00:01:59.260 --> 00:02:01.420
Yuki-san and Kurumi-san?

00:02:02.030 --> 00:02:05.000
What are you three wearing?!

00:02:05.000 --> 00:02:10.420
W-Well, Maria said you would enjoy this more.

00:02:10.580 --> 00:02:13.920
What nonsense is that horny
loli-succubus spouting now?!

00:02:14.310 --> 00:02:16.600
There you have it, Basara.

00:02:17.070 --> 00:02:19.800
So we'll be washing you, too.

00:02:23.120 --> 00:02:23.670
Huh?

00:02:44.260 --> 00:02:47.410
"Naughty Bath Time with Sexy Beauties"...

00:02:47.410 --> 00:02:51.210
Another gem has been added
to my treasured collection!

00:02:51.210 --> 00:02:52.710
Listen, you!

00:02:54.390 --> 00:02:55.960
How is it, Basara?

00:02:56.210 --> 00:02:58.030
D-Does it feel good?

00:02:58.030 --> 00:02:59.720
Y-Yeah.

00:03:00.580 --> 00:03:01.550
It does?

00:03:01.550 --> 00:03:02.720
Good.

00:03:03.010 --> 00:03:03.910
Mio.

00:03:05.700 --> 00:03:11.480
Henceforth we will fundamentally 
have no interaction with you all.

00:03:12.580 --> 00:03:15.220
With a military alliance
currently being formed

00:03:15.220 --> 00:03:18.230
between us and the reigning
demon-lord faction,

00:03:18.440 --> 00:03:21.000
we must avoid provoking useless 
suspicion and speculation

00:03:21.000 --> 00:03:25.240
that would come from making 
contact with you without cause.

00:03:25.550 --> 00:03:26.770
I understand.

00:03:26.770 --> 00:03:31.080
You can't let go of the peace 
you've finally obtained.

00:03:32.090 --> 00:03:33.820
That's all there is to discuss.

00:03:33.820 --> 00:03:36.170
You should return to your world.

00:03:39.390 --> 00:03:43.010
Are you planning to bid farewell 
to Mio without saying anything?

00:03:44.230 --> 00:03:45.260
Wilbert-san!

00:03:48.130 --> 00:03:49.520
Basara-dono.

00:03:49.830 --> 00:03:54.770
The attitude you've shown me and Mio 
thus far hasn't been a friendly one,

00:03:55.230 --> 00:03:57.770
but I tried thinking about it this way.

00:03:58.120 --> 00:04:02.200
Perhaps that was out of concern for Mio.

00:04:04.180 --> 00:04:09.160
The demon lord Wilbert feigned death
 from illness and disappeared,

00:04:09.160 --> 00:04:12.400
in order to stop the moderate faction
 that served him from going out of control.

00:04:14.180 --> 00:04:17.780
At the same time,
 he sent his daughter to the human realm,

00:04:17.780 --> 00:04:20.800
in order to protect her
 from the reigning demon lord.

00:04:21.800 --> 00:04:25.110
Then, while he watched over
his daughter in the human realm,

00:04:25.110 --> 00:04:27.450
he sought to ascertain 
how the conflict between

00:04:27.450 --> 00:04:30.780
the moderate faction and the reigning
demon-lord faction would fall,

00:04:30.780 --> 00:04:33.100
and thus he returned as another persona.

00:04:34.190 --> 00:04:35.880
That of the demon lord's brother.

00:04:38.070 --> 00:04:43.940
The gravity magic you used to rescue Mio
 was more than just power.

00:04:44.380 --> 00:04:47.920
There was a great kindness to it.

00:04:50.280 --> 00:04:53.740
Though maybe that's all my misunderstanding.

00:04:54.330 --> 00:04:55.230
Rukia-san?

00:04:55.900 --> 00:04:56.830
That's...

00:04:58.250 --> 00:05:00.330
Are you finished?

00:05:01.110 --> 00:05:04.800
You told quite a fantastical tale,

00:05:05.390 --> 00:05:06.840
but are you done now?

00:05:07.240 --> 00:05:07.920
Yes.

00:05:08.740 --> 00:05:12.160
That's just a convenient interpretation for me.

00:05:12.850 --> 00:05:15.850
I have no intention
 to tell Mio or anyone else.

00:05:18.120 --> 00:05:22.360
However, even if that's just
a fairy tale I dreamt up,

00:05:22.990 --> 00:05:28.110
thank you very much for protecting us...
 for protecting Mio all this time.

00:05:44.780 --> 00:05:46.000
Basara-dono.

00:05:47.970 --> 00:05:50.670
<i>From now on I'm protecting them.</i>

00:05:51.280 --> 00:05:53.640
<i>Both Mio and the others.</i>

00:06:11.720 --> 00:06:12.740
That's it!

00:06:12.740 --> 00:06:13.880
That's it!

00:06:13.880 --> 00:06:15.860
That's right!

00:06:15.860 --> 00:06:18.980
Now let's make this even more tantalizing!

00:06:18.980 --> 00:06:20.290
Click!

00:06:34.260 --> 00:06:36.600
No, what is this?

00:06:39.660 --> 00:06:42.230
My body's suddenly growing hot.

00:06:43.850 --> 00:06:44.480
Huh?

00:06:45.720 --> 00:06:46.940
Don't tell me...

00:06:47.300 --> 00:06:48.070
Maria!

00:06:50.770 --> 00:06:55.480
Seems that the special aphrodisiacs 
I whipped up are little too strong.

00:06:56.380 --> 00:06:57.580
Don't give me that!

00:07:01.130 --> 00:07:03.280
I'm going mad.

00:07:03.280 --> 00:07:05.490
You're so dirty, Onee.

00:07:09.850 --> 00:07:14.360
This is great as is!
 Or as they say in English, "no problem!"

00:07:14.360 --> 00:07:16.600
Now, let's keep it going!

00:07:35.990 --> 00:07:37.370
<i>Today it's going to be sunny!</i>

00:07:37.370 --> 00:07:41.790
<b>Today's Weather</b>

00:07:37.860 --> 00:07:39.890
<i>It's the perfect day for leisure!</i>

00:07:39.890 --> 00:07:41.790
<i>Let's enjoy the day!</i>

00:07:45.030 --> 00:07:46.780
I enjoyed today too much.

00:07:46.780 --> 00:07:48.380
What do you mean, "today"?!

00:07:48.900 --> 00:07:51.470
You're always going overboard!

00:07:52.880 --> 00:07:56.020
Basara and I were this close to...

00:07:56.020 --> 00:07:56.390
Huh?

00:07:57.060 --> 00:07:59.670
What are you muttering, Mio-sama?

00:07:59.670 --> 00:08:00.250
Huh?!

00:08:00.660 --> 00:08:02.870
I-It's nothing!

00:08:04.710 --> 00:08:06.730
Well, please eat up.

00:08:09.800 --> 00:08:11.440
Looks great again this morning!

00:08:11.730 --> 00:08:14.450
It doesn't look great. It <i>is</i> great.

00:08:15.680 --> 00:08:17.650
The eggs are sunny side up and runny,

00:08:17.650 --> 00:08:19.950
and the bacon is nice and crispy!

00:08:20.150 --> 00:08:24.350
It's a perfect breakfast that brings out
 the best of its ingredients.

00:08:24.350 --> 00:08:28.500
No, it's just the skill 
that all maids must have.

00:08:28.500 --> 00:08:30.960
This is indeed superb!

00:08:31.490 --> 00:08:36.520
To think my status as head of the Toujou 
household's kitchen would be in peril!

00:08:41.990 --> 00:08:43.940
This is seriously good.

00:08:43.940 --> 00:08:47.480
We're really lucky to eat breakfasts 
like this every morning!

00:08:49.510 --> 00:08:50.980
Thank you very much.

00:08:54.960 --> 00:08:58.570
Zest, starting tomorrow allow me
 to cook breakfast, as well.

00:08:58.570 --> 00:09:01.240
I'm pretty good at cooking, too.

00:09:01.710 --> 00:09:05.550
Huh? But I couldn't put you
 through the trouble.

00:09:05.550 --> 00:09:06.550
It's fine.

00:09:07.060 --> 00:09:10.550
I'm going to make Basara 
say mine's delicious, too!

00:09:11.250 --> 00:09:12.750
In that case, so will I.

00:09:13.140 --> 00:09:14.260
Me, too!

00:09:19.320 --> 00:09:24.210
In that case, why don't we take turns
 cooking from now on?

00:09:24.210 --> 00:09:25.540
Right, Basara-san?

00:09:25.540 --> 00:09:28.230
Well, I don't mind.

00:09:29.010 --> 00:09:30.520
Are you okay with that, Zest?

00:09:30.980 --> 00:09:33.780
Yes. If that's what everyone wishes.

00:09:34.190 --> 00:09:35.700
Then it's settled.

00:09:36.210 --> 00:09:37.280
I'm looking forward to it.

00:09:37.660 --> 00:09:39.690
Yeah, leave it to me.

00:09:39.690 --> 00:09:42.530
<i>Now, everyone,
 it's what you've been waiting for!</i>

00:09:42.780 --> 00:09:44.380
<i>It's always midsummer here!</i>

00:09:45.040 --> 00:09:48.720
<i>There are ocean waves,
 water slides, a flowing river,</i>

00:09:48.720 --> 00:09:53.190
<i>and a huge wave pool
 that can only be experienced here!</i>

00:09:52.420 --> 00:09:56.670
<b>Seiou Aqua Resort</b>

00:09:53.190 --> 00:09:55.060
<i>Seiou Aqua Resort!</i>

00:09:54.840 --> 00:09:59.550
<b>Grand Opening Today!</b>

00:09:55.060 --> 00:09:57.120
<i>Grand opening today!</i>

00:09:57.120 --> 00:09:59.550
<i>Come visit, everyone!</i>

00:10:01.130 --> 00:10:03.390
It's the middle of winter, so why?

00:10:05.810 --> 00:10:08.420
No, no, it's wonderful, isn't it?

00:10:08.420 --> 00:10:11.190
We now have a pool we can play in,
 even during the winter!

00:10:11.600 --> 00:10:13.820
Let's be happier about this!

00:10:14.050 --> 00:10:16.420
You're the only one happy about it.

00:10:16.420 --> 00:10:17.820
Because you can see people in swimsuits.

00:10:17.820 --> 00:10:18.820
Grk!

00:10:19.340 --> 00:10:22.870
Basara-san, you also want to see
 everyone in swimsuits, right?

00:10:23.270 --> 00:10:23.830
Huh?!

00:10:24.100 --> 00:10:26.110
Oh, uh, no, I...

00:10:26.110 --> 00:10:28.700
If you had to choose
 between seeing them or not,

00:10:28.700 --> 00:10:31.790
you'd choose seeing them, right?

00:10:33.400 --> 00:10:33.750
Well...

00:10:34.240 --> 00:10:35.840
Well, yeah.

00:10:36.350 --> 00:10:38.240
It's good that you're honest!

00:10:46.200 --> 00:10:49.350
<b>Seiou Aqua Resort</b>

00:10:47.970 --> 00:10:51.700
Wow! It's incredible!

00:11:03.620 --> 00:11:07.060
So this is one of the human realm's pools?

00:11:07.060 --> 00:11:08.360
It's impressive.

00:11:12.790 --> 00:11:14.130
This is awesome!

00:11:14.790 --> 00:11:16.320
Okay, over here, over here.

00:11:16.320 --> 00:11:18.320
Eyes over here, please!

00:11:20.980 --> 00:11:23.050
Huh? Toujou-kun?

00:11:24.230 --> 00:11:28.050
Tachibana? You're here, too, Kajiura-senpai?

00:11:28.050 --> 00:11:29.040
Yes.

00:11:29.040 --> 00:11:30.640
With everyone on the student council.

00:11:31.210 --> 00:11:32.640
What about you all?

00:11:32.980 --> 00:11:36.000
Yeah, we thought something like this
 would be nice for once.

00:11:36.500 --> 00:11:37.300
Right?

00:11:37.300 --> 00:11:38.040
Yeah.

00:11:39.010 --> 00:11:40.720
It's nice now and then.

00:11:41.120 --> 00:11:42.220
Listen, you.

00:11:43.850 --> 00:11:46.350
Tachibana, you look good in that.

00:11:46.350 --> 00:11:48.240
Y-You think so?

00:11:48.730 --> 00:11:52.660
If I knew you were coming,
 I would have worn something cuter.

00:11:53.050 --> 00:11:55.520
Hey, hey, what's going on here,

00:11:55.520 --> 00:11:58.950
all the usual suspects lined up together?

00:11:58.950 --> 00:12:00.130
Takigawa-kun?

00:12:00.130 --> 00:12:01.280
Takigawa?

00:12:01.280 --> 00:12:03.070
Hey, Basacchi!

00:12:03.070 --> 00:12:04.550
Why are you here?

00:12:05.300 --> 00:12:09.310
Quite the trend follower, 
coming here on your own.

00:12:09.690 --> 00:12:10.880
Huh?

00:12:10.880 --> 00:12:12.370
Come on, now.

00:12:12.370 --> 00:12:16.060
You think I'm here alone by choice?

00:12:17.600 --> 00:12:22.060
I'm here to keep an eye on you all,
 on behalf of the demon realm.

00:12:22.540 --> 00:12:26.990
Whenever you all go somewhere, 
I need to be nearby.

00:12:26.990 --> 00:12:28.330
So that's why.

00:12:28.690 --> 00:12:34.390
With that done, the main attractions here 
are the stupidly huge flowing pool over there,

00:12:34.390 --> 00:12:36.330
and the nation's longest water slide!

00:12:36.990 --> 00:12:39.840
You can eat at the food court
 on the west side!

00:12:39.840 --> 00:12:43.340
<b>Special: Thorough Guide to Seiou Aqua Re</b>

00:12:40.130 --> 00:12:43.340
I recommend the yakisoba 
packed with ingredients!

00:12:43.860 --> 00:12:46.260
You're a total trend follower.

00:12:46.260 --> 00:12:49.450
Anyway, let's all have fun today!

00:12:49.450 --> 00:12:51.150
Yeah!

00:13:04.020 --> 00:13:04.640
Huh?!

00:13:05.000 --> 00:13:05.600
Huh?

00:13:09.370 --> 00:13:10.370
Quick shots!

00:13:14.870 --> 00:13:16.310
<b>Blueberr
Ham, Cheese, and T
Tuna, Mayo
Caramel, Wh
Mango, Wh
Strawberry
Banana Cho</b>

00:13:22.350 --> 00:13:25.120
Hey, hey, what should we enjoy next?

00:13:25.120 --> 00:13:26.880
Well...

00:13:27.590 --> 00:13:30.390
By the way, where did Yuki and the others go?

00:13:30.390 --> 00:13:32.660
<b>Takoyaki</b>

00:13:30.390 --> 00:13:33.240
<b>Yakisoba</b>

00:13:30.390 --> 00:13:34.330
<b>Hot Takoyaki!</b>

00:13:30.390 --> 00:13:34.330
<b>Hamburgers</b>

00:13:30.390 --> 00:13:34.850
<b>Curry Rice</b>

00:13:30.390 --> 00:13:34.850
<b>Ramen</b>

00:13:30.800 --> 00:13:33.350
We got separated from them.

00:13:35.760 --> 00:13:38.980
<i>Then that means we're alone right now?</i>

00:13:49.920 --> 00:13:52.280
What a nice mood!

00:13:52.280 --> 00:13:57.710
Now, stop worrying about the others 
watching, and be more aggressive!

00:14:00.000 --> 00:14:00.880
Huh?

00:14:00.880 --> 00:14:02.970
Y-You're in the way!

00:14:02.970 --> 00:14:03.630
Huh?

00:14:04.140 --> 00:14:05.080
Hey, you.

00:14:05.080 --> 00:14:06.770
What are you doing?

00:14:06.770 --> 00:14:08.600
Photography is prohibited here.

00:14:08.600 --> 00:14:13.390
N-No, I was just adding
 to my Mio-sama collection.

00:14:13.630 --> 00:14:16.010
You can come to the security room with me.

00:14:16.010 --> 00:14:19.350
No! Hold on!

00:14:22.310 --> 00:14:23.070
Huh?

00:14:23.070 --> 00:14:24.900
Huh? A church?

00:14:26.580 --> 00:14:28.140
Yes, I do.

00:14:28.610 --> 00:14:32.530
Everyone, let's give a round of applause
 to celebrate their happy union!

00:14:34.230 --> 00:14:36.680
Wow. A wedding ceremony?

00:14:36.680 --> 00:14:38.620
So they host those here, huh?

00:14:38.980 --> 00:14:39.920
Yeah.

00:14:40.410 --> 00:14:41.530
Congratulations!

00:14:41.530 --> 00:14:42.460
So pretty.

00:14:42.930 --> 00:14:44.750
One day, I hope I...

00:14:51.460 --> 00:14:54.170
Oh? You two are also here?

00:14:55.140 --> 00:14:57.810
What a coincidence,
 running into you two here.

00:14:58.140 --> 00:14:59.650
Hasegawa-sensei.

00:14:59.650 --> 00:15:02.490
You're here for fun, too, Sensei?

00:15:02.490 --> 00:15:03.430
Yeah.

00:15:03.430 --> 00:15:05.070
For future reference.

00:15:05.500 --> 00:15:06.260
Yay!

00:15:06.260 --> 00:15:13.070
I need to be aware of such trends,
 in order to guide students as their teacher.

00:15:14.010 --> 00:15:15.190
What's the matter, Toujou?

00:15:15.780 --> 00:15:18.070
Your face is red. Do you have a fever?

00:15:18.070 --> 00:15:19.330
N-No.

00:15:22.080 --> 00:15:23.240
Hurry!

00:15:23.240 --> 00:15:24.080
Wait!

00:15:23.670 --> 00:15:25.060
Whoa, look out!

00:15:34.520 --> 00:15:37.990
You haven't forgotten your promise 
about this weekend, have you?

00:15:39.400 --> 00:15:40.100
No.

00:15:40.900 --> 00:15:42.360
Then see you later, Toujou.

00:15:42.360 --> 00:15:43.240
You, too, Naruse.

00:15:52.970 --> 00:15:53.920
Mio?!

00:15:59.170 --> 00:16:02.140
Having my memory card stolen is the worst!

00:16:02.140 --> 00:16:05.630
What do they think
 someone's precious collection is?!

00:16:05.930 --> 00:16:08.250
Good thing I thought this might happen!

00:16:09.540 --> 00:16:12.630
Huh? Basara-san? Mio-sama?

00:16:14.960 --> 00:16:16.990
Is it the curse of the Master-Servant pact?

00:16:18.250 --> 00:16:20.100
I need to relieve you quickly.

00:16:21.230 --> 00:16:23.520
Is there anywhere we can hide?

00:16:27.180 --> 00:16:29.140
Wait here for a moment.

00:16:30.070 --> 00:16:32.070
Where can we avoid being seen?

00:16:32.070 --> 00:16:33.220
Basara-san!

00:16:33.220 --> 00:16:34.030
Maria?

00:16:36.020 --> 00:16:38.840
The curse is hitting her quite strongly.

00:16:39.640 --> 00:16:43.040
If you don't make Mio-sama submit
at once, she'll be in danger!

00:16:48.230 --> 00:16:49.100
Damn it!

00:16:50.350 --> 00:16:51.490
Basara-san?!

00:16:53.750 --> 00:16:55.570
This feels great!

00:16:55.570 --> 00:16:56.470
Yeah!

00:17:00.130 --> 00:17:01.730
That felt really great, didn't it?

00:17:01.730 --> 00:17:02.730
Yeah, it did.

00:17:06.020 --> 00:17:07.990
This flowing river's great, isn't it?

00:17:07.990 --> 00:17:08.680
Yeah.

00:17:08.680 --> 00:17:10.040
Mio, we're doing it.

00:17:10.040 --> 00:17:11.910
Huh? Here?

00:17:11.910 --> 00:17:12.690
Yeah.

00:17:12.690 --> 00:17:16.110
Everyone's focused on the pool, 
so they won't notice us.

00:17:16.110 --> 00:17:17.180
But...

00:17:17.180 --> 00:17:19.540
I'll do what I can to keep others
 from noticing us.

00:17:20.070 --> 00:17:21.820
So you do your best, too.

00:17:25.540 --> 00:17:26.460
All right.

00:17:27.140 --> 00:17:29.400
Please, Onii-chan.

00:17:29.400 --> 00:17:30.220
Okay.

00:17:31.370 --> 00:17:32.880
S-Sorry.

00:17:32.880 --> 00:17:34.710
Huh? Naruse-san?

00:17:35.800 --> 00:17:37.310
You two are here, too?

00:17:37.900 --> 00:17:41.240
The flowing river feels great, doesn't it?

00:17:41.240 --> 00:17:42.580
Right, Toujou-kun?

00:17:42.580 --> 00:17:44.720
Y-Yes, it does.

00:17:44.720 --> 00:17:46.600
It really does.

00:17:47.200 --> 00:17:49.740
It'll be too late if we wait for them to go.

00:17:49.740 --> 00:17:50.660
I'm starting.

00:17:58.140 --> 00:18:00.370
Naruse-san? Is something wrong?

00:18:01.060 --> 00:18:03.020
No, it's nothing.

00:18:03.020 --> 00:18:04.940
A-Are you sure?

00:18:06.580 --> 00:18:07.490
Our balance!

00:18:08.980 --> 00:18:10.250
What are you doing?!

00:18:10.250 --> 00:18:12.910
Keep your voice down as much as possible.

00:18:13.360 --> 00:18:16.260
Yeah, I know.

00:18:52.920 --> 00:18:54.710
Are you all right, Naruse-san?

00:18:55.290 --> 00:18:57.170
Huh? Where's Toujou-kun?

00:19:02.030 --> 00:19:03.080
It's a wave!

00:19:03.080 --> 00:19:04.730
We're getting washed away!

00:19:12.110 --> 00:19:14.230
<i>We're almost there, Mio!</i>

00:19:16.120 --> 00:19:18.010
<i>I'm going to...</i>

00:19:28.850 --> 00:19:31.250
There came the climax!

00:19:32.590 --> 00:19:34.170
That was incredible, wasn't it?

00:19:34.170 --> 00:19:35.000
Yes.

00:19:36.260 --> 00:19:38.760
Speaking of which, where are those two?

00:20:00.070 --> 00:20:03.280
Onii-chan, I'm going to...

00:20:12.360 --> 00:20:14.420
Ah, that was fun!

00:20:14.420 --> 00:20:16.020
Y-Yeah.

00:20:16.580 --> 00:20:19.550
Though it was a bit embarrassing at the end.

00:20:20.890 --> 00:20:24.510
I can't believe I missed out
 on capturing such a sweet scene!

00:20:24.510 --> 00:20:26.820
I'm a failure of a succubus!

00:20:26.820 --> 00:20:27.800
What are you talking about?

00:20:29.120 --> 00:20:30.250
Basara.

00:20:30.250 --> 00:20:31.810
Next time, do it with me, as well.

00:20:32.080 --> 00:20:34.690
When you do, you can do something
 more incredible than you did with Mio.

00:20:34.690 --> 00:20:35.810
Give me a break.

00:20:36.370 --> 00:20:39.070
It was a miracle we didn't caught this time.

00:20:39.610 --> 00:20:42.820
Still, it was fun.

00:20:42.990 --> 00:20:43.610
Huh?

00:20:45.370 --> 00:20:46.320
Yeah.

00:20:47.140 --> 00:20:48.800
Let's go again, yeah?

00:20:49.550 --> 00:20:50.340
Of course.

00:20:50.340 --> 00:20:53.580
And when we do, please wear
my special selection of swimsuits!

00:20:53.790 --> 00:20:55.730
No. I refuse.

00:20:55.730 --> 00:20:57.590
No way!

00:20:57.590 --> 00:20:59.770
Mio-sama!

00:20:59.770 --> 00:21:01.540
I know they're nothing good!

00:21:01.540 --> 00:21:03.590
That's not true!

00:21:04.160 --> 00:21:07.590
<i>I hope days like these can last forever.</i>

00:21:11.630 --> 00:21:13.100
Are you all right, Mio-sama?!

00:21:13.400 --> 00:21:14.090
That's—

00:21:14.090 --> 00:21:15.960
Stand back, Basara-sama!

00:21:16.900 --> 00:21:18.020
Wait, Zest.

00:21:18.920 --> 00:21:22.130
That's a sacred bird
 used by the hero village.

00:21:22.130 --> 00:21:23.110
The hero village?

00:21:30.280 --> 00:21:31.120
Let me see.

00:21:37.540 --> 00:21:40.280
That was rather violent 
for an ordinary letter.

00:21:40.280 --> 00:21:41.130
They're orders.

00:21:43.490 --> 00:21:44.230
Yuki?

00:21:44.890 --> 00:21:46.810
We've been ordered to return.

00:21:46.810 --> 00:21:48.130
Both me and Kurumi.

00:21:49.040 --> 00:21:50.660
Why would they order that?

00:21:50.660 --> 00:21:53.670
Well, a lot of things have happened lately.

00:21:53.670 --> 00:21:57.230
Maybe the elders have decided 
they can't overlook it anymore.

00:21:57.230 --> 00:21:59.150
There's more to our orders.

00:21:59.550 --> 00:22:03.380
We're to bring Basara and 
Mio with us on our return.

00:22:04.010 --> 00:22:05.280
Me and Basara, too?

00:22:05.280 --> 00:22:07.440
The hero village wants Mio-sama?

00:22:07.440 --> 00:22:08.650
What's the meaning of this?

00:22:09.480 --> 00:22:10.990
<i>I figured this would come.</i>

00:22:16.400 --> 00:22:17.660
I see.

00:22:18.070 --> 00:22:23.430
Seems that those elders of the hero village
 have started making their move.

00:22:23.430 --> 00:22:24.670
What shall we do?

00:22:25.280 --> 00:22:28.930
If necessary, I shall head there again.

00:22:29.280 --> 00:22:30.220
No.

00:22:30.220 --> 00:22:33.810
In fact, if we act carelessly, 
we might make things worse.

00:22:34.120 --> 00:22:37.060
However, we can't just leave this be.

00:22:37.720 --> 00:22:41.060
We don't know what kind of danger
 Maria might face.

00:22:42.190 --> 00:22:43.500
She'll be fine.

00:22:44.390 --> 00:22:47.140
Let's leave this in his hands.

00:22:56.530 --> 00:22:59.920
Take the necessary measures 
if it comes down to it, huh?

00:23:00.660 --> 00:23:05.090
What shall we do now, huh, Basacchi?

00:23:06.420 --> 00:23:08.180
We can't do this!

00:23:08.180 --> 00:23:10.590
The elders are definitely plotting something,

00:23:10.950 --> 00:23:13.590
asking for us to bring 
Basara-niichan and Mio!

00:23:14.250 --> 00:23:16.600
Can we not just ignore this?

00:23:17.980 --> 00:23:21.100
You're right. That would be one option.

00:23:21.400 --> 00:23:27.620
But considering our future,
 this isn't such a simple matter.

00:23:29.710 --> 00:23:32.550
The elders sense a threat.

00:23:32.550 --> 00:23:35.220
An equilibrium has been maintained
 ever since the war,

00:23:35.220 --> 00:23:37.620
but they're afraid that the balance 
between heroes and demons

00:23:37.920 --> 00:23:40.620
will be toppled because of us.

00:23:46.880 --> 00:23:48.380
That doesn't mean we can do this!

00:23:48.830 --> 00:23:51.430
Letting Mio-sama go to the hero village!

00:23:51.430 --> 00:23:52.370
Maria.

00:23:53.200 --> 00:23:56.140
Do you have any idea how dangerous 
that will be for Mio-sama?

00:23:56.850 --> 00:24:00.140
The commotion in the demon realm 
was finally settled, and now—

00:24:00.560 --> 00:24:04.200
Just leave us alone already!

00:24:06.060 --> 00:24:06.910
Maria.

00:24:09.290 --> 00:24:10.400
Don't worry.

00:24:10.760 --> 00:24:14.910
No matter what happens, I'll protect you all.

00:24:21.410 --> 00:24:22.160
Basara.

00:24:34.770 --> 00:24:36.180
Sorry to keep you waiting.

00:24:37.560 --> 00:24:39.680
No, you're right on time.

00:24:40.160 --> 00:24:41.390
You came for me.

00:24:42.100 --> 00:24:43.010
I'm happy.

00:24:44.940 --> 00:24:48.420
Sorry. I'm sure you're also busy
 with many things.

00:24:48.420 --> 00:24:51.300
No! We made the promise 
a while back, after all.

00:24:51.970 --> 00:24:55.450
I let Mio and the others know
 ahead of time that I was heading out.

00:24:56.100 --> 00:24:58.450
I see. In that case...

00:25:01.140 --> 00:25:04.530
You're all mine until tomorrow morning.

00:25:16.090 --> 00:25:16.970
Mio-sama?

00:25:17.660 --> 00:25:21.360
W-Wow, this daikon's so thick and hard!

00:25:21.360 --> 00:25:23.470
I bet it would taste good served as oden!

00:25:24.220 --> 00:25:28.530
I should increase my cooking repertoire
 before Basara comes home.

00:25:28.530 --> 00:25:30.230
I want to surprise him after all!

00:25:31.070 --> 00:25:32.230
Mio-sama...

00:25:33.990 --> 00:25:35.740
Oh, these look good, too!

00:26:20.490 --> 00:26:25.330
Hey, shouldn't we return, just you and me?

00:26:25.890 --> 00:26:28.480
We just need to persuade the elders anyway.

00:26:29.900 --> 00:26:32.590
If that's what Basara desired.

00:26:33.400 --> 00:26:35.330
But that's not the case.

00:26:36.160 --> 00:26:40.810
Basara would never let us go alone.

00:26:41.490 --> 00:26:45.320
But if Basara-niichan returns 
to the village, that means...

00:26:53.930 --> 00:26:56.400
That's too cruel.

00:26:57.460 --> 00:27:01.550
Even so, we can't afford
 not to return in our current situation.

00:27:10.150 --> 00:27:12.540
Hey, are you serious about that?

00:27:15.050 --> 00:27:17.630
You sound like you've
gone back to the old you.

00:27:18.300 --> 00:27:21.860
Hiding how you truly feel while you suffer.

00:27:22.500 --> 00:27:26.780
Sorry, but you wouldn't 
understand our suffering.

00:27:30.660 --> 00:27:31.620
Onee...

00:27:34.420 --> 00:27:35.900
Mio-sama...

00:27:39.740 --> 00:27:42.420
Good grief, how dedicated.

00:27:45.540 --> 00:27:46.160
Toujou.

00:27:47.480 --> 00:27:48.020
Huh?

00:27:48.660 --> 00:27:49.950
Thinking again?

00:27:50.700 --> 00:27:53.470
Your head was in the clouds
 during our time on the train, as well,

00:27:54.290 --> 00:27:58.210
but you promised to think only about me
 until tomorrow morning, right?

00:27:58.210 --> 00:27:59.610
I'm sorry.

00:28:00.600 --> 00:28:02.240
Is there something troubling you?

00:28:02.240 --> 00:28:02.980
Yes.

00:28:03.610 --> 00:28:06.720
There are several things that I
suddenly need to make a decision on.

00:28:07.370 --> 00:28:09.440
And those things are important issues

00:28:09.440 --> 00:28:14.160
not just to you, but others
as well, aren't they?

00:28:14.160 --> 00:28:15.520
Y-Yes.

00:28:17.060 --> 00:28:17.900
Very much so.

00:28:20.520 --> 00:28:22.990
In that case, I'll let you in
 on a good way to think about it.

00:28:24.940 --> 00:28:25.740
Huh?

00:28:25.980 --> 00:28:28.990
If you're in a dilemma because
the problems aren't just your own,

00:28:30.050 --> 00:28:33.750
then think of their problems
 as if they were your own, as well.

00:28:34.420 --> 00:28:37.940
Do that and you'll be able to decide
 what it is you want to do.

00:28:37.940 --> 00:28:38.870
But that would—

00:28:38.870 --> 00:28:44.650
Of course, your decisions aren't necessarily 
going to be good for every single person.

00:28:45.570 --> 00:28:47.010
That includes yourself, too.

00:28:47.640 --> 00:28:49.940
However, that's exactly why you need

00:28:49.940 --> 00:28:52.680
to steel yourself and have
an unwavering resolve.

00:28:53.380 --> 00:28:55.270
Unwavering resolve?

00:28:55.620 --> 00:28:56.220
Yeah.

00:28:57.040 --> 00:28:58.580
That way, the decisions you make

00:28:58.580 --> 00:29:03.610
will be ones both you and another 
can be proud of and won't regret.

00:29:05.450 --> 00:29:07.460
Was that a little helpful?

00:29:07.460 --> 00:29:08.310
Yes.

00:29:08.310 --> 00:29:09.280
Thank you very much.

00:29:09.720 --> 00:29:14.260
In that case, could you start focusing on me?

00:29:14.820 --> 00:29:16.790
From now until tomorrow morning.

00:29:23.880 --> 00:29:24.670
Yes.

00:29:44.570 --> 00:29:46.580
No way, that...

00:29:46.580 --> 00:29:47.570
Toujou!

00:30:03.270 --> 00:30:04.870
Th-That's...

00:30:14.870 --> 00:30:17.110
No, if you keep going...

00:30:22.630 --> 00:30:24.130
N-No!

00:30:25.670 --> 00:30:27.360
I-It's not what you think.

00:30:50.490 --> 00:30:51.430
Toujou!

00:30:52.390 --> 00:30:53.420
Toujou!

00:30:57.420 --> 00:30:58.550
Toujou!

00:30:58.550 --> 00:31:00.730
I'm going to...

00:31:14.460 --> 00:31:16.310
Yuki, do you have a moment?

00:31:17.350 --> 00:31:18.160
Come in.

00:31:19.940 --> 00:31:20.660
Where's Yuki?

00:31:21.170 --> 00:31:23.430
Onee said she was taking a shower.

00:31:23.430 --> 00:31:24.190
I see.

00:31:25.850 --> 00:31:26.740
Huh?

00:31:27.190 --> 00:31:28.670
What's this?

00:31:30.800 --> 00:31:34.660
Wow, everyone's so cute!

00:31:34.660 --> 00:31:36.330
My, yes they are.

00:31:36.330 --> 00:31:37.570
It's a nice photo.

00:31:37.570 --> 00:31:38.930
Everyone has a good smile.

00:31:39.760 --> 00:31:43.060
Because it was taken
 before that incident happened.

00:31:43.060 --> 00:31:43.940
Huh?

00:31:44.310 --> 00:31:47.460
I think we were always smiling
 back in those days.

00:31:48.380 --> 00:31:51.310
Basara-niichan, Onee, and myself, all of us.

00:31:52.060 --> 00:31:53.250
I see.

00:31:53.250 --> 00:31:55.650
It's a side of you all I don't know.

00:31:55.650 --> 00:31:56.460
Mio...

00:31:59.820 --> 00:32:00.870
Maria.

00:32:00.870 --> 00:32:01.730
Yes?

00:32:10.100 --> 00:32:10.970
Basara!

00:32:18.940 --> 00:32:21.220
Basara-niichan!

00:32:25.290 --> 00:32:26.110
<i>Basara.</i>

00:32:28.230 --> 00:32:31.250
What do you think you're doing, Yuki?

00:32:31.250 --> 00:32:32.690
Elder.

00:32:32.690 --> 00:32:36.990
Those two have been exiled 
from the hero village.

00:32:37.270 --> 00:32:39.920
But you're going to live as a hero.

00:32:39.920 --> 00:32:42.920
You will not be allowed
 to interact with them anymore!

00:32:48.070 --> 00:32:52.480
<i>I couldn't chase after him back then.</i>

00:32:53.080 --> 00:32:54.220
<i>I couldn't protect him.</i>

00:32:54.650 --> 00:32:57.390
<i>Not during his most painful moments.</i>

00:32:59.950 --> 00:33:03.440
<i>I'm sure Basara will comply 
with the Elders' orders,</i>

00:33:03.440 --> 00:33:05.520
<i>to protect us all,</i>

00:33:05.760 --> 00:33:08.360
<i>without regard for his own suffering.</i>

00:33:08.360 --> 00:33:10.650
<i>I can't just tell Basara not 
to go when he's like that.</i>

00:33:11.560 --> 00:33:16.130
<i>I don't have any right to say that,
 when I couldn't say anything back then.</i>

00:33:16.130 --> 00:33:18.080
Why are you worrying about this
 all on your own?

00:33:21.830 --> 00:33:22.540
Mio.

00:33:23.160 --> 00:33:27.430
You've been thinking of Basara
 both then and now,

00:33:27.430 --> 00:33:29.470
but you're putting a lid on those feelings?

00:33:30.810 --> 00:33:33.050
You're really dumb.

00:33:34.930 --> 00:33:37.620
It's fine. You can be more honest.

00:33:37.620 --> 00:33:38.430
Huh?

00:33:39.280 --> 00:33:42.930
I know you all have a regret
 from your past you can't erase.

00:33:42.930 --> 00:33:48.440
I can't just casually claim to understand 
how much you've suffered because of it.

00:33:48.440 --> 00:33:50.460
But still, I want you to tell me.

00:33:50.460 --> 00:33:52.920
I want to hear how you truly feel.

00:33:52.920 --> 00:33:53.940
Why?

00:33:54.330 --> 00:33:58.180
You saved me many times during
our time in the demon realm, right?

00:33:58.180 --> 00:33:59.950
Both you and Kurumi-chan.

00:34:00.820 --> 00:34:02.950
So it's my turn now.

00:34:10.300 --> 00:34:12.960
This is your homeland, isn't it?

00:34:14.740 --> 00:34:17.250
I want to go.

00:34:17.250 --> 00:34:18.430
To the hero village.

00:34:18.770 --> 00:34:19.700
Huh?

00:34:19.700 --> 00:34:21.060
Please, Yuki.

00:34:21.060 --> 00:34:22.930
Don't bear this all on your own.

00:34:23.160 --> 00:34:24.530
Let me help you.

00:34:25.180 --> 00:34:27.930
If anything happens to you, then I'd—

00:34:30.450 --> 00:34:34.620
I want to help Basara, too.

00:34:37.800 --> 00:34:39.180
I want to know.

00:34:39.180 --> 00:34:44.790
I want to know what suffering you, 
Kurumi-chan, and Basara have been carrying.

00:34:45.660 --> 00:34:49.640
Because I believe that's necessary 
for me to help you three.

00:34:50.300 --> 00:34:51.380
Mio...

00:34:51.380 --> 00:34:55.690
After all, Basara's your most
precious childhood friend.

00:34:56.230 --> 00:35:01.220
And Basara's the most precious
Onii-chan in the world to me.

00:35:06.950 --> 00:35:12.600
The truth is, I don't want 
to see Basara suffer anymore!

00:35:12.600 --> 00:35:14.230
Yeah, I know.

00:35:15.240 --> 00:35:19.520
If that destiny is unavoidable, 
then let's stand against it together.

00:35:20.160 --> 00:35:23.780
That way we can all save Basara
 together this time.

00:35:23.780 --> 00:35:24.400
Yeah.

00:35:48.470 --> 00:35:51.560
Sorry. For slipping into your mind
 without permission.

00:35:52.250 --> 00:35:53.520
Maria's doing?

00:35:53.970 --> 00:35:54.570
Yeah.

00:35:55.020 --> 00:35:57.440
Because I wanted to have 
a proper talk with you.

00:35:58.050 --> 00:35:59.780
Without hiding anything.

00:36:01.440 --> 00:36:02.620
You're so pushy.

00:36:04.640 --> 00:36:09.070
Jeez. With the two of them that amped up,
 we have no choice but to go.

00:36:19.170 --> 00:36:20.040
Basara.

00:36:20.670 --> 00:36:23.070
You should do as you please.

00:36:23.820 --> 00:36:25.900
But please don't forget this:

00:36:26.400 --> 00:36:28.680
you have me on your side.

00:36:29.310 --> 00:36:31.470
I'll grant you some of my power.

00:36:31.950 --> 00:36:35.190
For you, and for the future of you all.

00:36:42.180 --> 00:36:47.870
Basara, no matter what happens,
 I'm on your side.

00:37:10.020 --> 00:37:11.050
Sensei?

00:37:12.400 --> 00:37:14.140
Good morning, Basara.

00:37:14.970 --> 00:37:16.520
Good morning.

00:37:23.900 --> 00:37:27.410
<b>Local - Takahatafudo
Limited Express - Keio Hachioji</b>

00:37:37.310 --> 00:37:39.510
"An unwavering resolve," huh?

00:37:41.140 --> 00:37:44.640
<i>It's true that we can't avoid 
returning to the hero village</i>

00:37:44.640 --> 00:37:47.410
<i>if we want to protect our future.</i>

00:37:47.410 --> 00:37:48.550
<i>But...</i>

00:38:02.580 --> 00:38:03.840
<i>Am I afraid?</i>

00:38:04.330 --> 00:38:05.900
<i>Of returning there?</i>

00:38:06.640 --> 00:38:09.240
<i>Of facing my past?</i>

00:38:11.270 --> 00:38:12.100
Damn it!

00:38:12.100 --> 00:38:13.800
You finally returned.

00:38:15.680 --> 00:38:16.730
Takigawa?

00:38:18.030 --> 00:38:18.680
Hey!

00:38:25.380 --> 00:38:26.260
Looks good!

00:38:27.060 --> 00:38:29.630
Sorry for making you treat me.

00:38:29.630 --> 00:38:32.840
Surprised you can say that
 after planning on it from the start.

00:38:32.840 --> 00:38:33.780
Well, yeah.

00:38:33.780 --> 00:38:36.520
Oh, this one to this one are my pieces.

00:38:37.020 --> 00:38:38.830
So, what are you going to do?

00:38:38.830 --> 00:38:40.270
About the hero village.

00:38:41.620 --> 00:38:43.020
What are you talking about?

00:38:43.350 --> 00:38:44.340
Hey, hey.

00:38:44.340 --> 00:38:47.020
Do you think we don't know
 anything about that?

00:38:50.670 --> 00:38:54.120
This is a matter between
members of the hero clan.

00:38:54.120 --> 00:38:56.290
It has nothing to do with you demons.

00:38:56.660 --> 00:38:59.500
We'll protect our daily life
 with our own hands.

00:39:00.290 --> 00:39:03.540
Oh, this one's grilled up good.

00:39:04.790 --> 00:39:06.800
I appreciate the nice spirit,

00:39:07.260 --> 00:39:09.830
but things are finally getting settled 
between the moderate faction

00:39:09.830 --> 00:39:12.370
and the reigning demon-lord faction.

00:39:14.260 --> 00:39:18.770
There will trouble for us
 if anything happens at a time like this,

00:39:18.770 --> 00:39:21.490
due to you all getting emotional 
and acting on your own.

00:39:25.900 --> 00:39:29.450
Basacchi, I think you have
the wrong impression here.

00:39:29.450 --> 00:39:34.570
I'm here to keep an eye on you,
 not be your best friend.

00:39:35.560 --> 00:39:36.130
Yeah.

00:39:36.820 --> 00:39:38.880
Then you understand, don't you?

00:39:38.880 --> 00:39:41.910
We're just leaving Naruse Mio in your care.

00:39:41.910 --> 00:39:46.090
If she's put in danger,
 then we'll eliminate that threat.

00:39:46.300 --> 00:39:49.490
We'll destroy your hometown if necessary,

00:39:52.610 --> 00:39:57.790
and it's none of our concern if you
all lose this meager happiness of yours.

00:40:00.220 --> 00:40:02.270
We'll erase them completely.

00:40:02.270 --> 00:40:04.270
That's my job, after all.

00:40:06.020 --> 00:40:09.370
Overcooked meat just isn't worth eating.

00:40:09.370 --> 00:40:10.780
Are you serious about that?

00:40:10.970 --> 00:40:12.040
Yeah.

00:40:12.040 --> 00:40:13.790
You seriously got to be careful.

00:40:14.870 --> 00:40:16.070
Takigawa...

00:40:17.530 --> 00:40:18.640
It's done!

00:40:22.000 --> 00:40:23.620
We made a lot.

00:40:24.660 --> 00:40:26.880
We might have gone a bit overboard.

00:40:26.880 --> 00:40:27.950
It doesn't matter.

00:40:27.950 --> 00:40:29.670
Basara's coming home.

00:40:30.460 --> 00:40:33.800
Still, Basara-sama's late.

00:40:41.670 --> 00:40:42.560
Kurumi?

00:40:43.250 --> 00:40:48.160
We're like wives waiting for our husband.

00:40:49.860 --> 00:40:51.620
I'd be happy if we were.

00:40:52.670 --> 00:40:55.090
You're getting ahead of yourselves.

00:40:55.090 --> 00:40:56.620
We haven't even married him yet.

00:40:56.940 --> 00:41:00.950
Good idea! Let's do that!

00:41:01.380 --> 00:41:02.140
Huh?

00:41:12.890 --> 00:41:14.750
Has to be here, doesn't it?

00:41:15.270 --> 00:41:15.920
Yeah.

00:41:16.650 --> 00:41:19.070
It's the second time we've fought, isn't it?

00:41:19.070 --> 00:41:20.970
No, the third.

00:41:21.270 --> 00:41:22.240
That so?

00:41:27.780 --> 00:41:29.640
Now no one will interfere.

00:41:30.310 --> 00:41:31.540
Let's get started.

00:41:31.540 --> 00:41:32.480
Yeah.

00:42:17.650 --> 00:42:18.900
Takigawa!

00:42:18.900 --> 00:42:23.330
I won't let even you lay a hand
 on our peaceful lives or our future!

00:42:23.720 --> 00:42:26.530
So that's your will? Your pride?

00:42:26.530 --> 00:42:29.540
However, can you really protect that?

00:42:29.540 --> 00:42:32.590
When you're a coward 
trembling at your own past!

00:42:37.940 --> 00:42:39.090
What?!

00:42:58.950 --> 00:43:00.120
What?!

00:43:00.120 --> 00:43:02.820
The hero village?!

00:43:06.740 --> 00:43:08.500
See? Look at that.

00:43:13.700 --> 00:43:15.920
You won't let anyone lay a hand on it?

00:43:15.920 --> 00:43:18.380
Don't go spouting crap you can't back up!

00:43:18.690 --> 00:43:21.060
The only reason you've survived
 this long is that

00:43:21.060 --> 00:43:25.390
your clever tricks
 miraculously happened to work out!

00:43:25.800 --> 00:43:27.060
Screw you!

00:43:35.200 --> 00:43:38.720
You should learn your place already!

00:43:43.930 --> 00:43:45.390
That's it, then?

00:43:56.410 --> 00:43:59.760
Nice facing yourself for once, isn't it?

00:44:01.260 --> 00:44:02.540
Don't underestimate me!

00:44:04.400 --> 00:44:05.390
Take this!

00:44:11.240 --> 00:44:13.300
I can't use Banishing Shift?!

00:44:26.080 --> 00:44:27.190
Hey, now.

00:44:27.190 --> 00:44:29.540
Have your skills gone dull
 from all that peace?

00:44:29.930 --> 00:44:34.040
<i>Or is something happening within Basacchi?</i>

00:44:42.420 --> 00:44:45.650
Well, doesn't matter to me.

00:45:11.480 --> 00:45:12.350
What?

00:45:12.350 --> 00:45:13.660
Done already?

00:45:14.100 --> 00:45:15.830
Oh, well.

00:45:15.830 --> 00:45:18.310
Guess I'll deliver the finishing blow now.

00:45:22.820 --> 00:45:27.010
Don't worry. We'll take Naruse 
and the others into our care.

00:45:29.390 --> 00:45:30.400
Basara.

00:45:40.880 --> 00:45:41.870
Oh?

00:45:41.870 --> 00:45:48.140
You're right. It might be a miracle
 that we've made it through everything so far.

00:45:48.920 --> 00:45:51.730
We borrowed power from
a lot of different people, too.

00:45:51.730 --> 00:45:54.720
But that's not all.

00:45:55.700 --> 00:45:58.610
We never gave up,
 no matter what happened.

00:45:59.180 --> 00:46:00.880
We had faith in ourselves.

00:46:01.420 --> 00:46:03.130
And we fought!

00:46:03.470 --> 00:46:07.130
That's why we're here right now!

00:46:10.750 --> 00:46:11.650
Come!

00:46:30.180 --> 00:46:31.030
What?!

00:46:35.060 --> 00:46:38.960
I'm going to protect their smiles myself,
 no matter what!

00:47:00.630 --> 00:47:04.480
I have never once given up on our future!

00:47:04.810 --> 00:47:07.960
Takigawa!

00:47:25.920 --> 00:47:27.370
Jeez.

00:47:27.370 --> 00:47:33.210
Looks like you haven't slacked off just because
 problems with the demons are settling down.

00:47:35.140 --> 00:47:36.510
Takigawa.

00:47:36.820 --> 00:47:38.320
Do you as you please.

00:47:38.320 --> 00:47:41.770
I'll be watching to see how
far that will of yours can go.

00:47:42.580 --> 00:47:43.550
That guy...

00:47:51.610 --> 00:47:52.530
I'm home.

00:47:56.100 --> 00:47:56.630
Huh?

00:47:58.220 --> 00:47:59.520
Welcome home.

00:48:01.940 --> 00:48:03.040
Wh-What are you...

00:48:03.480 --> 00:48:05.410
Well? Surprised?

00:48:08.180 --> 00:48:09.890
Y-Yeah.

00:48:11.370 --> 00:48:12.430
That's all?

00:48:12.730 --> 00:48:15.430
No, you all look pretty.

00:48:15.430 --> 00:48:16.590
Really pretty.

00:48:20.740 --> 00:48:25.180
I was fine, but everyone insisted.

00:48:25.180 --> 00:48:29.570
Oh ho? You were pretty
into this, too, Kurumi-san.

00:48:29.570 --> 00:48:32.700
You were saying,
 "I'll finally get to be Basara-niichan's bride!"

00:48:33.470 --> 00:48:35.510
Huh? Then you mean these are...

00:48:35.510 --> 00:48:36.260
Yes.

00:48:36.260 --> 00:48:40.500
Maria suggested we should
all become your brides,

00:48:40.500 --> 00:48:43.640
in order to strengthen
our bonds as your family.

00:48:43.920 --> 00:48:45.960
Don't you think it's a great idea?

00:48:46.260 --> 00:48:51.710
The Master-Servant pact makes everyone
stronger when their bonds are stronger!

00:48:52.140 --> 00:48:56.220
Doing this will make all of us even stronger!

00:48:56.740 --> 00:48:59.720
With this, we should be fine
 even if we do return to the village.

00:49:01.430 --> 00:49:02.380
You all...

00:49:03.640 --> 00:49:04.780
I...

00:49:04.780 --> 00:49:08.640
I knew it. You were planning on going 
to the hero village all by yourself.

00:49:08.640 --> 00:49:09.230
Huh?

00:49:09.580 --> 00:49:12.400
The other day you said,

00:49:12.930 --> 00:49:17.070
No matter what happens, I'll protect you all.

00:49:17.470 --> 00:49:20.050
Not "we," but "I."

00:49:20.050 --> 00:49:23.960
So I thought that might be so.

00:49:25.940 --> 00:49:27.000
Why?

00:49:27.790 --> 00:49:31.460
You always, always go into
the most danger all by yourself.

00:49:31.770 --> 00:49:34.660
Are we that bad?

00:49:37.430 --> 00:49:39.490
Do you have that little faith in us?!

00:49:44.600 --> 00:49:45.750
Mio-sama!

00:49:45.750 --> 00:49:47.850
Mio, your curse...

00:49:48.130 --> 00:49:50.200
Of course it would.

00:49:50.200 --> 00:49:52.750
No matter how much I may be thinking of you,

00:49:53.330 --> 00:49:57.740
my desire to go with you is still selfish.

00:49:58.150 --> 00:50:00.620
But I need to say it.

00:50:01.130 --> 00:50:05.250
Otherwise, you'll go on your own.

00:50:05.830 --> 00:50:11.560
The hero village probably believes
 I'm the root of their current problem.

00:50:12.120 --> 00:50:13.950
So I should just go by myself.

00:50:14.920 --> 00:50:16.130
If I do...

00:50:16.430 --> 00:50:20.590
Then maybe me, Kurumi, 
and Mio can avoid harm.

00:50:21.170 --> 00:50:23.710
You're right that that is a possibility.

00:50:24.290 --> 00:50:27.950
But that's your own selfish belief.

00:50:27.950 --> 00:50:30.830
I'll never let you do that.

00:50:34.500 --> 00:50:35.150
Yuki?!

00:50:35.620 --> 00:50:38.070
Why are you being this rash?!

00:50:38.070 --> 00:50:39.850
Isn't it obvious?

00:50:40.340 --> 00:50:43.530
Because this is about you!

00:50:43.810 --> 00:50:45.910
Onee and Mio are both serious about this.

00:50:46.410 --> 00:50:48.820
No, it's not just those two.

00:50:49.790 --> 00:50:54.550
Basara-niichan, this is how
 all five of us feel!

00:50:56.760 --> 00:50:58.800
Maria. Kurumi.

00:50:59.420 --> 00:51:05.330
Basara-sama, just as you
treasure us above all else,

00:51:05.330 --> 00:51:08.810
we treasure you, as well.

00:51:08.810 --> 00:51:12.500
Even if you tell us "no," we won't give up.

00:51:12.500 --> 00:51:16.190
We'll follow you, even if it
means disobeying your orders!

00:51:16.500 --> 00:51:23.380
So please forgive our selfish desire
 to accompany you.

00:51:27.670 --> 00:51:28.480
Zest?!

00:51:28.900 --> 00:51:30.710
Please, Basara,

00:51:31.220 --> 00:51:33.550
make us submit.

00:51:34.220 --> 00:51:37.020
Make us stronger.

00:51:37.820 --> 00:51:40.220
Until you can rest assured.

00:51:41.180 --> 00:51:41.960
Mio...

00:51:42.980 --> 00:51:47.210
Kurumi-san and I will help you, of course.

00:51:47.210 --> 00:51:48.600
Right, Kurumi-san?

00:51:57.470 --> 00:52:00.740
Please, Onii-chan, do it.

00:52:08.220 --> 00:52:09.100
All right.

00:52:10.900 --> 00:52:11.680
Mio.

00:52:13.920 --> 00:52:14.710
Yuki.

00:52:17.280 --> 00:52:18.250
Kurumi.

00:52:20.200 --> 00:52:20.970
Maria.

00:52:23.550 --> 00:52:24.460
Zest.

00:52:24.460 --> 00:52:25.440
Basara-sama.

00:52:27.740 --> 00:52:30.640
I'll relieve you now.

00:52:45.550 --> 00:52:48.390
Basara, me, too.

00:52:48.390 --> 00:52:50.040
Yeah, I know.

00:52:56.100 --> 00:52:59.170
Basara, me, too!

00:53:04.800 --> 00:53:07.180
Basara-niichan, me, too.

00:53:07.610 --> 00:53:11.330
I'll be your partner before Basara-san.

00:53:11.330 --> 00:53:12.350
Maria?

00:53:15.110 --> 00:53:16.750
Oh, Maria!

00:53:31.490 --> 00:53:35.090
Basara-niichan, does it feel good?

00:53:35.090 --> 00:53:37.580
Am I doing it properly?

00:53:37.830 --> 00:53:41.220
You're doing well, Kurumi-san.

00:53:46.260 --> 00:53:48.340
You shouldn't let your guard down.

00:53:52.620 --> 00:53:57.350
This is our wedding, isn't it?

00:53:57.960 --> 00:54:00.610
Yeah, it is.

00:54:00.870 --> 00:54:04.560
In that case, I have this for us!

00:54:14.380 --> 00:54:16.230
Maria, what's this?

00:54:17.100 --> 00:54:20.990
Instead of a rice shower, 
it's an aphrodisiac shower!

00:54:20.990 --> 00:54:24.460
To celebrate overcoming 
the Succubus's baptism!

00:54:24.770 --> 00:54:27.540
J-Jeez, Maria!

00:54:31.980 --> 00:54:34.220
Please, Onii-chan!

00:54:34.680 --> 00:54:36.350
I'm yearning for it!

00:54:36.660 --> 00:54:38.040
Me, too!

00:54:39.100 --> 00:54:41.890
Come to me, Basara-niichan!

00:54:42.910 --> 00:54:44.130
Basara-sama!

00:54:46.620 --> 00:54:47.890
Basara-san!

00:54:50.340 --> 00:54:52.410
Yeah. Here I go.

00:55:53.780 --> 00:55:57.160
I'm never letting you go.

00:56:00.020 --> 00:56:01.170
Sorry about that.

00:56:02.660 --> 00:56:05.760
We are family, after all.

00:56:10.170 --> 00:56:10.900
Yeah.

00:56:44.150 --> 00:56:45.300
Good morning.

00:56:45.300 --> 00:56:46.020
Huh?

00:56:46.720 --> 00:56:48.470
How long are you going to keep us waiting?

00:56:48.470 --> 00:56:50.050
It's an important day.

00:56:50.050 --> 00:56:52.030
Yeah. Sorry, sorry.

00:56:54.940 --> 00:56:55.530
Hm?

00:56:56.030 --> 00:56:58.770
We're perfectly packed now!

00:56:58.770 --> 00:57:01.120
Are you sure
 that isn't a bit too big for you?

00:57:04.680 --> 00:57:05.840
It's done!

00:57:06.980 --> 00:57:08.770
There, perfect!

00:57:08.770 --> 00:57:09.550
Mio?

00:57:09.930 --> 00:57:11.550
Oh, good morning!

00:57:12.260 --> 00:57:13.800
Did you make all these?

00:57:14.330 --> 00:57:17.230
If you had said something,
I would have made them.

00:57:17.230 --> 00:57:18.160
It's fine.

00:57:18.160 --> 00:57:21.060
I was in charge of breakfast 
this morning, anyway.

00:57:21.300 --> 00:57:23.500
Well? Perfect, aren't they?

00:57:23.500 --> 00:57:26.260
They look really normal, though.

00:57:26.260 --> 00:57:28.960
I would have made character bento.

00:57:30.060 --> 00:57:31.070
What?

00:57:37.680 --> 00:57:39.670
Yeah, it's good!

00:57:39.670 --> 00:57:40.580
Right?

00:57:40.890 --> 00:57:43.720
In that case, I'll try some, too!

00:57:43.720 --> 00:57:44.660
Me, too!

00:57:44.660 --> 00:57:46.170
I was hungry!

00:57:46.170 --> 00:57:47.810
No, no!

00:57:47.810 --> 00:57:50.820
There's no point to the bento
 if you eat them here!

00:57:51.640 --> 00:57:53.590
Mio-sama, so stingy!

00:57:54.650 --> 00:57:56.590
That's my share, isn't it?

00:57:56.590 --> 00:57:59.220
Mio, what's wrong with a little bit?

00:57:59.220 --> 00:58:01.600
I told you "no"!

00:58:06.770 --> 00:58:07.850
It's about time to head out.

00:58:08.900 --> 00:58:09.680
Yes!

00:58:29.080 --> 00:58:30.820
<i>Don't look back at the past.</i>

00:58:31.370 --> 00:58:32.470
<i>Look toward tomorrow,</i>

00:58:32.470 --> 00:58:33.760
<i>toward hope,</i>

00:58:33.760 --> 00:58:34.730
<i>toward the future.</i>

00:58:35.620 --> 00:58:37.790
<i>We're going to seize it.</i>

00:59:21.380 --> 00:59:23.850
Hurry up and get here, Basara.

00:59:24.340 --> 00:59:29.110
The past that will never go away
 is waiting for you.
